WEBVTT

00:00:03.206 --> 00:00:06.895
Under Start with an event, let's pick the Content Published Event.

00:00:06.895 --> 00:00:11.556
The first event you add becomes the start activity, and its card shows a Start badge.

00:00:12.037 --> 00:00:15.002
Its settings open at the bottom of the canvas.

00:00:15.002 --> 00:00:18.479
Content Types limits the event to the types you choose.

00:00:18.479 --> 00:00:22.527
Let's pick Article, so other content does not start the workflow.

00:00:23.009 --> 00:00:25.759
Each activity shows its outcomes as ports.

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:29.942
Let's point at the Done port, where a plus sign appears, then click

00:00:29.942 --> 00:00:31.719
it and search for Notify.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:33.972
Let's select Notify Task.

00:00:33.972 --> 00:00:38.020
It is added to the right, connected to Done by a transition, and

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:40.680
it displays a notification when it runs.

00:00:41.131 --> 00:00:45.420
A message is required, so the card and the Issues tab flag a problem.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:49.481
Let's type a message and leave the field, and the problem clears.

00:00:49.936 --> 00:00:53.717
The designer saves your changes as a draft while you work, and a

00:00:53.717 --> 00:00:55.067
draft does not run.

00:00:55.067 --> 00:00:58.956
Let's select Publish, which makes the draft the version that runs.

